.TH CLOPS_LS 1 "May 2026" "v2.0.1a" "CamClops - Manifest/Trip ls"
.SH NAME
clops_ls \- non-interactive trip lister for CamClops manifests
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B clops_ls
.RB [ \-\-format= \fIfmt\fR ]
.RB [ \-\-fields= \fIf1,f2,...\fR ]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.RI [ MID " | " MID : TID ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B clops_ls
lists dashcam trips from cached CamClops manifests.  It is the scriptable,
pipe-friendly alternative to
.BR "camclops \-t" " and " "camclops \-T" .
All output goes to
.BR stdout ;
errors go to
.BR stderr .
.PP
Without arguments,
.B clops_ls
prints a one-line summary for every trip across all manifests, grouped under
a manifest header line.  A
.I MID
argument filters output to one manifest.  A
.IR MID : TID
argument prints a full detail block for a single trip.
.PP
Both
.I MID
and
.I TID
are case-insensitive.  Ambiguous characters are normalised
.RB ( O\(→0 ,
.BR I\(→1 ,
.BR L\(→1 ).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-format= fmt
Structured output format.  Valid values:
.BR json ,
.BR csv ,
.BR xml .
.B \-\-format=json
is equivalent to
.BR \-\-json .
.B csv
emits a header row followed by one row per trip.
.B xml
emits one
.B <trip>
element per trip inside a
.B <trips>
root.
.TP
.BI \-\-fields= f1,f2,...
Comma-separated list of fields to include in
.B csv
or
.B xml
output (ignored for json).
Available fields:
.BR manifest_id ,
.BR trip_id ,
.BR date ,
.BR start_time ,
.BR start_epoch ,
.BR duration ,
.BR duration_seconds ,
.BR segment_count ,
.BR note ,
.BR start_lat ,
.BR start_lon ,
.BR end_lat ,
.BR end_lon ,
.BR distance_km ,
.BR distance_mi ,
.BR gps_lock_seconds ,
.BR gps_track_status .
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit JSON instead of text.  Equivalent to
.BR \-\-format=json .
With no filter, outputs an array of manifest objects each containing a
.B trips
array.  With
.IR MID : TID ,
outputs a single trip object.  Suitable for piping to
.BR jq (1).
.TP
.B \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the CamClops version string and exit.
.TP
.B \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.SH "DEFAULT OUTPUT FORMAT"
Without
.BR \-\-json ,
output is a header row followed by a separator, then one line per trip:
.PP
.RS
.nf
MID TID Date        Start     Duration  Segs  Distance  GPS
----------------------------------------------------------------
[CY]  /z/srcdash/ex10
CY  7E  2026-02-25  04:44:24  18m 29s   7     22.7 km   pts
CY  0Y  2026-02-25  13:56:53  42m 6s    15    56.8 km   pts
.fi
.RE
.PP
Columns:
.TP
.B MID
Two-character manifest ID.
.TP
.B TID
Two-character trip ID within the manifest.
.TP
.B Date
Trip date in
.I YYYY-MM-DD
format.
.TP
.B Start
Trip start time in
.I HH:MM:SS
format (local time from filename timestamps).
.TP
.B Duration
Human-readable trip duration (e.g.\&
.IR "39m 52s" ).
.TP
.B Segs
Number of video segments in the trip.
.TP
.B Distance
Crow-flies haversine distance between the trip start and end GPS coordinates.
Displayed in km or miles depending on the
.B useImperial
preference.  Shows
.B \-
if no GPS coordinate data is available for the trip.
.TP
.B GPS
GPS data availability indicator:
.RS
.TP
.B track
Full per-second GPS track has been extracted (via
.B camclops\ \-G
or
.BR clops_gpsexport (1)).
Ready for GPX/KML/GeoJSON export.
.TP
.B pts
Start and end coordinates only, captured automatically during the initial
.B \-s
scan.  Sufficient for distance calculation; run
.BR clops_gpsexport (1)
to extract the full route.
.TP
.B \-
No GPS data.  Typically a cold-start stub segment where the GPS receiver
never acquired a fix.
.RE
.SH "DETAIL OUTPUT (MID:TID)"
.PP
.RS
.nf
Trip:       X1:87
Date:       2026-02-09
Start:      04:38:38
Duration:   39m 52s
Segments:   14
Seg dur:    180s
Manifest:   /z/srcdash/ex2/clops_manifest_X1.json
Source:     /z/srcdash/ex2
Start pos:  30.419000, -89.025191
End pos:    30.367684, -89.613496
Distance:   56.7 km
GPS:        complete  (lock: 0s)
.fi
.RE
.PP
.B Duration
shows the computed ffprobe duration in parentheses if available:
.I "39m 52s  (ffprobe: 39m 51s)" .
.B GPS
shows the track status and GPS lock time in seconds if it has been scanned
by
.BR "clops_gpsinfo \-\-scan\-all\-trips" .
.SH "JSON OUTPUT"
.PP
With
.BR \-\-json ,
the output is a JSON array of manifest objects.  Each trip object contains:
.PP
.RS
.nf
{
  "id": "87",
  "date": "2026-02-09",
  "start_time": "04:38:38",
  "duration": "39m 52s",
  "segment_count": 14,
  "segdur": 180,
  "distance_km": 56.71,
  "start_lat": 30.419,
  "start_lon": -89.025,
  "end_lat": 30.367,
  "end_lon": -89.613,
  "gps_status": "complete",
  "gps_lock_sec": 0,
  "duration_ffprobed": -1,
  "note": ""
}
.fi
.RE
.PP
.B distance_km
is
.B \-1
if no GPS coordinates are available.
.B duration_ffprobed
is
.B \-1
if the ffprobe duration has not yet been computed.
.B gps_lock_sec
is
.B \-1
if GPS has not been extracted for that trip.
Lock time is populated automatically when GPS is extracted (via
.BR "camclops \-G" ,
.BR clops_gpsexport (1),
or the GUI GPS tab) and can also be batch-populated across all trips with
.BR "clops_gpsinfo \-\-scan\-all\-trips" .
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
List all trips across all manifests:
.B clops_ls
.TP
List trips for manifest X1 only:
.B clops_ls X1
.TP
Show detail for one trip:
.B clops_ls X1:87
.TP
JSON output for all manifests, extract trip IDs with jq:
.B "clops_ls --json | jq '.[] | .trips[] | .id'"
.TP
JSON output for one manifest:
.B clops_ls --json X1
.TP
Find all trips with full GPS tracks:
.B "clops_ls --json | jq '.[] | .trips[] | select(.gps_status == \"complete\") | .id'"
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/camclops/manifests.json
Manifest index listing all known manifests.
.TP
.I ~/.config/camclops/camclops.json
Application settings (
.B useImperial
controls distance display units).
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
No manifests found, unknown MID, or unknown TID.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR camclops (1),
.BR clops_gpsinfo (1),
.BR clops_gpsexport (1),
.BR clops_probe (1),
.BR clops_audit (1),
.BR clops_videos (1)
